Why AGPL, recorded so it stays a choice rather than a discovery (ADR-013):

  monopoly-core is AGPL-3.0 and is imported as a library, which forms a
  combined work. Section 13 extends the source disclosure obligation to users
  who interact with the software over a network, which is exactly how Ledger
  is delivered. The obligation is therefore to offer source to anyone using
  the hosted instance. For a project built to demonstrate capability that is
  close to zero cost and arguably a benefit.

  The documented exit, if commercialisation ever becomes real, is to drop
  Monopoly and use the pdfplumber parsers instead. ADR-002 keeps that path
  alive deliberately.

